MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_001: This village suffered a lot of damage. But everyone\nis trying so hard to move on from it.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_002: Today, I helped the villagers develop new farmland.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_003: The fields were buried under so much rubble we\nwere plowing the wasteland.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_004: Oh! I perform tricks for the kids! And, sometimes,\nI help with the cooking.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_005: I can only help everyone in my time between battles,\nso it's not doing that much but still...
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_006: <NCA>"It sounds like a lot, actually."
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_007: <NCB>"You're working very hard."
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_008: <ACA>W-well, I mean, I'm not the type of person who's that\ninto battles anyway...
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_009: <ACB>N-no, not at all! I just enjoy helping out around the\nvillage is all.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_010: Living an ordinary life between battles is how I \nlike to rest.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_011: When I'm laughing with everyone, I forget that I'm\ntired or strung out. Is that weird, maybe?
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_012: What a lovely smile. You know, Promised One,\nyou're a really kind person.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_013: You're so brave and strong in battle. It makes me\nkinda, well...
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_014: <NCA>"You were scared of me?"
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_015: No, not really! Well. Maybe. A little.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_016: At first, just knowing you were the Herald of the Pale\nRaven felt so overwhelming...
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_017: Just seeing you used to make me nervous. B-but now,\neverything's different.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_018: I know you now. You're kindhearted, you're warm,\nand you care about this small village and its people.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_019: I know you're someone just like us.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_020: Unless, I mean, that's a rude thing to say. Maybe?
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_021: <NCA>"They're kind words."
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_022: <NCB>"Let's continue to work side by side."
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_023: <ACA>I'm— I'm so glad to hear that!
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_024: <ACB>Y-yes!
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_A_025: Well, bye! I'm going to go help the villagers for a bit!
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_001: "Do not despair. The Herald of the Pale Raven shall\nreveal their presence to you."
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_002: Please let the Promised One return...\nPromised One?
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_003: Ah! P-Promised One! You're back! Thank goodness!
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_004: <NCA>"Did you call for me?"
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_005: Yes! I just knew you'd come back.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_006: I was reading Poems of Prophet Jehoshaphat and\nperforming a spell to summon you.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_007: Although... If you don't already know that, then\nmaybe it was pointless to do?!
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_008: Well, I was just doing what the villagers told me\nto do! They said it'd bring you back!
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_009: Please don't laugh...
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_010: Why do I still feel intimidated?
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_011: I can't believe the legendary Herald wants to talk\nto me. But it happens, over and over.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_012: <NCA>"I came just to see you."
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_013: Wh-what? You did? Thank you so much.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_014: Promised One, is your role in all this over now?
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_015: <NCA>"There are still people who need help."
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_016: <NCB>"My work continues."
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_017: I knew you'd say something like that.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_018: I... I'm not going to follow you. I'm sorry, but I'm just\na normal person. I don't... I...
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_019: You're stronger and kinder than anyone else, and\nyou're everyone's hero. You know that?
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_020: <NCA>"I am sorry I'm leaving."
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_021: <NCB>"We'll meet again someday."
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_022: <ACA>No, please, you don't have to apologize.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_023: <ACB>Aw, you're really kind.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_024: <RSDS>Please do come back though! Even if it's just, you\nknow, sometimes. I'll be waiting to see you.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_025: And you don't gotta come to visit as the "Herald."\nYou can just come and be you. I'd like that.
MID_SE_Ism_Hal_S_026: I'll be waiting for you!